Current execution model:

```text
User case:
    ./scripts/build.sh
        ↓
    cases/user/User_default.json
        ↓
    CIRRUS
        ↓
    SimulationRunner
        ↓
    CIRRUS/output

Verification:
    ./scripts/build.sh --verification
        ↓
    cases/verification/verification_suite.json
        ↓
    VerificationRunner
        ↓
    verification outputs / diagnostics
```

Supported command-line usage:

```text
./scripts/build.sh
./scripts/build.sh --norun
./scripts/build.sh --verification
./scripts/build.sh --config <case.json>
./scripts/build.sh --plot
./scripts/build.sh --log
```

Design goals:

* User cases should run without modifying source code
* Verification cases should remain isolated from normal user simulations
* Configuration paths should resolve relative to the project rather than the build directory
* User-facing output should be written under the project-level `output/` directory
* Platform-specific execution details should remain outside solver logic

